From f5e7537f99cd1565687c4ec5085406eeae1a7428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anon <anon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:20:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] windows.devices: add the Bluetooth LE stack

Add the Wine Bluetooth LE support on Linux, from the driver up to the WinRT
classes an application uses.

winebth.sys is a root-enumerated bus driver that owns the BlueZ connection:
it exposes radio and remote-device PnP objects, drives discovery, connect,
pairing and GATT through libdbus, and reports device and advertisement events
to the caller through a shared event ring. New IOCTLs cover LE discovery,
connect/disconnect, pairing and unpairing, GATT reads, writes and
notifications, and the LE state.

On top of it, windows.devices.bluetooth implements the WinRT surface:
BluetoothLEDevice and BluetoothAdapter, advertisement and advertisement
watchers, GATT services, characteristics and descriptors, GattSession,
BluetoothDeviceId and BluetoothUuidHelper, plus the acceleration and
signal-strength filter types. windows.devices.radios implements the radio
runtime class, windows.devices.enumeration enumerates devices through COM and
drives pairing and unpairing, and bluetoothapis gains
BluetoothGATTSetCharacteristicValue. wintypes adds the DataReader and
DataWriter runtime classes the GATT buffers are read and written with.

Two supporting fixes are included because the stack depends on them:
RoGetAgileReference no longer starts RPC remoting for agile objects, which
deadlocked on the loader lock when a WinRT event handler was registered while
another DLL was loading, and IoDeleteDevice clears the child list it frees so
a later bus-relations query cannot walk freed memory.
